Mix.Sync.Lock: make a new port file, not a write through a hard link

The first lock in a new lock directory gets lock_0 as a hard link of
its port_P file, and port_P stays. A later lock that gets the same
ephemeral port P wrote port_P in place, so lock_0 named its own live
port. The probe of lock_0 then reached its own accept loop, and the
process waited for itself ("held by process" with its own PID).

Remove port_P before the write, so that the write makes a new file.

--- a/lib/mix/lib/mix/sync/lock.ex
+++ b/lib/mix/lib/mix/sync/lock.ex
@@ -174,6 +174,10 @@
     port_path = Path.join(path, "port_#{port}")
     os_pid = System.pid()
 
+    # A port file from an earlier lock with the same port can still be a
+    # hard link of lock_N. Remove it, so that the write below makes a new
+    # file and does not change lock_N.
+    _ = File.rm(port_path)
     switch_file_create!(port_path, encode_lock_info(port, os_pid))
 
     case grab_lock(path, port_path, 0) do
